      "How To:Play VideoPlay Video00:35How to Remove Screens from Your Old Hickory ShedHow to Remove Screens from Your Old Hickory Shed",
      "Many Old Hickory sheds include screened windows to improve ventilation while keeping insects out. If you need to remove the screens for cleaning, replacement, or seasonal airflow, the process is simple and requires minimal tools.",
      "Start by opening the shed window fully to access the interior screen frame. Most Old Hickory window screens are secured with spring clips or small retaining tabs. Gently compress the clips or release the tabs and pull the screen frame inward toward you. Avoid forcing the frame, as excessive pressure can bend the aluminum edging.",
      "Once removed, inspect the screen mesh and frame for debris or damage. Clean with mild soap and water, allow to dry completely, and reinstall by reversing the process, ensuring the frame sits flush and secure within the window track.",
      "Proper maintenance of shed window screens improves airflow, extends screen life, and keeps your storage shed, workshop, or backyard building functioning efficiently year-round.",
      "Play VideoPlay Video00:41How to Adjust the Doors on Your Old Hickory Shed – Video GuideHow to Adjust the Doors on Your Old Hickory Shed – Video Guide",
      "This video walk-through demonstrates how to properly adjust the doors on your Old Hickory shed to maintain smooth operation and proper alignment. Watch as we cover common door alignment concerns, hinge positioning, and latch alignment to ensure your shed doors open and close correctly.",
      "If your shed doors are sticking, sagging, or not sealing evenly, this video provides a clear visual overview of the adjustment process specific to Old Hickory shed construction. Designed for shed owners in Massachusetts and New England, this guide helps you better understand your building’s door hardware and overall performance.",
      "Add-Ons:Play VideoPlay Video00:43Add Shelving to Your Old Hickory ShedAdd Shelving to Your Old Hickory Shed",
      "Maximize storage capacity inside your Old Hickory shed by adding custom shelving designed for durability and organization. Built-in shed shelving helps keep tools, lawn equipment, seasonal decorations, hardware, and workshop supplies off the floor while improving accessibility and interior efficiency.",
      "Shelving systems can be configured to match your shed size, wall height, and intended use. Options include full-length wall shelving, reinforced heavy-duty shelves for power tools and equipment, multi-tier storage layouts, and corner shelving to optimize unused space.",
      "Whether your shed functions as a backyard storage building, garden shed, workshop, or hobby space, professionally installed shelving increases usable square footage and keeps your structure organized year-round. Designed to integrate seamlessly with Old Hickory framing systems, shelving upgrades add long-term functionality and value to your shed investment.",
      "Play VideoPlay Video00:50Add a Workbench to Your Old Hickory ShedAdd a Workbench to Your Old Hickory Shed",
      "Upgrade your Old Hickory shed with a built-in workbench designed to transform standard storage space into a functional workshop. A professionally installed shed workbench creates a dedicated surface for tools, repairs, woodworking projects, hobby equipment, and small machinery while maximizing interior organization.",
      "Workbench upgrades can be customized to match your shed size, wall height, and layout. Options include full-length wall-mounted benches, reinforced framing for heavier equipment, and configurations that preserve floor space for larger storage needs.",
