      "Important Questions You Should Ask:Dog KennelsSheds - Greenhouses - Garages - Animal StructuresSaunas - Office Sheds - CabinsGeneralAre the kennels easy to clean?",
      "Yes. Interior wall finishes are designed for durability and easy maintenance. Smooth, moisture-resistant surfaces make routine cleaning and sanitizing simple, helping you maintain a healthy environment for your dogs.",
      "What exterior siding and roofing options are available?",
      "Chateau Sheds offers multiple siding choices, including painted engineered siding or stained board-and-batten styles. Roofing options include architectural shingles, with metal roof upgrades available for added durability. Windows, doors, and decking upgrades are also available to customize the appearance and function of your kennel.",
      "Do you handle building permits?",
      "We provide the necessary drawings and structural information to assist with permitting; however, it is the customer’s responsibility to submit documentation and obtain approval from their local municipality.",
      "What site preparation is required?",
      "Your kennel site must be properly leveled and prepared before delivery. Most customers hire a local contractor to handle grading, tree removal if necessary, and foundation preparation.",
      "What type of foundation is required?",
      "A properly prepared concrete or compacted gravel pad is required prior to delivery. The size of the foundation must match the overall dimensions of your kennel structure. We recommend a professionally installed pad to ensure long-term stability.",
      "Will you connect the electrical system?",
      "Kennels can be pre-wired with electrical packages; however, final electrical connections must be completed by a licensed local electrician in accordance with local codes.",
      "Will you connect water or plumbing?",
      "Any plumbing, water supply, or drain connections must be completed by a licensed plumber after delivery. Chateau Sheds does not perform on-site plumbing work.",
      "Can the kennel be placed directly on the ground?",
      "No. A properly prepared foundation is required before delivery. Elevating the structure on a solid base improves drainage, climate control, and long-term durability.",
